            <ArticleTitle>Diffuse coronary arteriodysplasia in a Holstein-Friesian cow.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>207-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The coronary arteries of a 6-year-old Holstein-Friesian cow showed dysplastic lesions characterized by the following vascular changes: irregular, aneurysmal dilation; intimal fibrosis associated with myointimal cells; aberrant internal elastic lamina; oedema and mast cell infiltrates; and variation in the thickness of the media, including tortuosity with irregular dilation of the lumen of the artery and a plexiform structure formed from the right coronary artery.</AbstractText>
